--
A constructor template's constraint evaluates an is_convertible probe whose
parameter copy-initialization needs another class's converting constructor
template.  Nested re-entry of the template-constructor conversion fallback is
now permitted inside a substitution (sfinae_context_depth), not only inside
a constant-expression context, which sfinae_contextt suspends.  Distilled
from cpp17_unique_ptr_derived_return failing with libstdc++ 11 (whose
is_convertible is the SFINAE probe, not the __is_convertible builtin).
